{
  "_why": "ONEWAY1ai-i (D228; the oneway design §11): Daoris's one command tree, `daoris …`, declared once. `doctrine` are the CLI's commands, offline, at the root; every group is the desktop's program's, which the CLI hands every other word to, whole. A group's `verbs` are its sub-verbs, `takes` what it reads where no sub-verb is named, `whole` a group whose words its own command judges, and `nested` a sub-verb's own sub-verbs. `moved` names each old form and the form it is now: refused, exit 2, doing nothing. `flags` names each flag that has one name now, by the verb that takes it. Held equal to the driver's `CommandWords` (CommandWordsTests) and the CLI's command table (cli-tree.test.ts); `reconcile` is CONTEXTONE1b's, which the CLI fills in.",
  "doctrine": ["analyze", "check", "doctor", "index", "init", "reconcile", "status", "sync", "upstream"],
